    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-15055",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.47)$ given below, compute $P(1 \\leq X \\lt 5).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0222\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.4015\\,$ | $\\,0.7107\\,$ | $\\,0.9163\\,$ | $\\,0.9892\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0\\})+P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0)+P(1\\le X<5) \\\\  & =F(0)+P(1\\le X<5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X<5) & =F(4)-F(0) \\\\  & =0.9163-0.0222 \\\\  & =0.8941.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14129452/observations/step-e15055-3733d813d171beeb6faf.html",
